      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Alpha-atrial natriuretic peptide (ANP) levels, plasma renin activity, and plasma aldosterone levels were measured in 103 patients with coronary heart disease (CHD) having signs of various circulatory failures. The parameters were studied in relation to central hemodynamic values, and their dependence on the stage of chronic circulatory failure. Alpha-ANP was found to be one of the factors of the humoral systems implicated in the pathogenesis of chronic circulatory failure in CHD patients. The plasma level of alpha-ANP was found to be related to the state of the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system both in healthy subjects and CHD patients."},
